# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Next.js application. Claude Code runs **inside** the app container, so it has no docker CLI —
everything on this page is yours to run from the host. The commands Claude uses from inside are
in [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).

## First run

```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```

The container installs dependencies on boot and then starts the dev server under supervisord.
The app is at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).

`.env` carries your `UID`/`GID` so container-written files stay owned by you. `.env.local` holds
the database credentials — start from `.env.local.example`.

## Working in the container

```bash
docker compose exec app claude   # Claude Code
docker compose exec app bash     # a shell
docker compose down              # stop
```

## Packages

Install inside the container, never on the host — `.npmrc` sets `ignore-scripts=true` there, so a
malicious postinstall script cannot reach your machine. `node_modules/` is shared through the
volume mount, so the host sees the result either way.

```bash
docker compose exec app npm install <package>
```

## Dev server

It runs under supervisord so it can be restarted without restarting the container — restarting the
container would kill any Claude Code session inside it.

```bash
docker compose exec app supervisorctl -c supervisord.conf restart next-dev
docker compose exec app supervisorctl -c supervisord.conf status
docker compose logs -f app
```

The supervisor RPC interface is published on `127.0.0.1:9001`.

## Handy aliases

```bash
alias dcup='docker compose up -d'
alias dcdown='docker compose down'
alias dcclaude='docker compose exec app claude'
alias dcsh='docker compose exec app bash'
```
